  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Vetriviera, located in the Castelli shopping complex at 448 boulevard du Mercantour in Nice, is a well-established practice on the French Riviera, with a medical team covering several specialties (medical imaging, orthopaedic surgery, dermatology, ophthalmology...). A reassuring address if you're travelling with your dog in the Nice area.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic presents itself as operating 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, with an on-call vet available at all times for emergency consultations and a second practitioner available for surgical emergencies — a claim echoed by the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office website and several vet directories, which, however, merely relay this same original statement rather than verifying it independently. Client reviews offer a more concrete clue: a phone welcome praised during a 1am call for a cat's cystitis, a cat saved after a trauma that occurred at midnight. These testimonials show genuine night-time care in these specific cases, without guaranteeing permanent 24/7 availability. One review also qualifies the experience, mentioning a wait described as "endless" for news during a busy period — a comment on waiting time, not on an emergency going unhandled. This makes it an option worth keeping in mind if your dog needs care outside regular hours during your stay in Nice.</p>
      <div class="callout"><svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg> Emergencies: the clinic presents itself as open 24/7. A call before heading over is still recommended to confirm availability at the exact moment you need it.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The clinic is located in the Ariane district, in the north-east of Nice, not far from the motorway and the main roads crossing the city.</p>
